#. Tag: title
#: final-word.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Final word from the Author"
msgstr "Završna riječ autora"

#. Tag: title
#: final-word.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who am I, what is my business?"
msgstr "Ko sam ja, koje je moje zanimanje?"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"My employer is Danka Deutschland GmbH, a leading and manufacturer-"
"independent provider of professional and hi-speed digital printing systems, "
"black-and-white as well as color. Danka provides hardware, software, "
"service, maintenance, consumables and customized solutions for the products "
"in its portfolio. I work there as a System Engineer. Amongst the brands "
"Danka offers are Heidelberg (formerly Kodak), Canon, &Hewlett-Packard;, "
"Hitachi, Infotec and EfI."
msgstr ""
"Moj poslodavac je Danka Deutschland GmbH, vodeći i nezavisni proizvođački "
"nabavljač profesionalnih hi-speed digitalnih štampačkih sistema, crno-"
"bijelih i u boji. Danka nabavlja hardver, softver, servis, održavanjem "
"potrošni materijal i prilagođena rješenja u portfoliju. Radim kao sistemski "
"inženjer. Brendovi koje Danka nudi su Heidelber (bivši Kodak), Canon, "
"&Hewlett-Packard;, Hitachi, Infotec i Efl."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"My acquaintance with &Linux; and the Free Software community is not too old. "
"When I started to play around with &Linux; at the beginning of 1999, my "
"deepest disappointment was the poor support for printing. True, I made all "
"our machines spit out simplex prints -- but what about duplex? What about "
"punching the output? How to make sorting work? Or stapling, cover sheets and "
"all the other beautiful finishing options our engines offer to customers? No "
"way -- at least for me as a non-geek!"
msgstr ""
"Moje poznanstvo sa &Linux; i Free Software zajednicom nije mnogo staro. Kada "
"sam se počela igrati sa &Linux; na poletku 1999, moje najveće razočarenje je "
"bila slaba podrška za štampanje. Istina, moje mašine su printale "
"jednostrano, ali šta je sa dvostranim štampanjem?  Kako napraviti "
"sortiranje , da radi? Ili heftanje, naslovne strane i ostale prekrasne "
"završne opcije koje naši inženjeri nude mušterijama? Nemoguće -- barem za "
"nekoga ko nije štreber, poput mene."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I began a search on the Internet for a solution. Fortunately not much later, "
"in May 1999, Mike Sweet, principal developer of &CUPS;, announced the first "
"Beta release of this superb piece of printing software. After trying it "
"briefly, I knew this was it!"
msgstr ""
"Počela sam pretraživati internet u potrazi za rješenjem. Srećom ne mnogo "
"kasnije, u maju 1999, Mike Sweet, glavni developer &CUPS; -a,  najavio je "
"prvu Beta verziju ovog vrhunskog komada štampačeg softvera. Nakon "
"kratkotrajnog isprobavanja, znala sam da je to bilo to!"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next thing I attempted: to make &Linux; distributions interested in this new "
"stuff. Believe me -- it was more than tenacious! They seemed to think they "
"already had the best thing they could get in printing. One reason probably "
"was that they (and many &Linux; developers) never had to think about how to "
"best support a printer duplexer -- because one had never come near their own "
"desks..."
msgstr ""
"Sljedeća stvar koju sam probala: napraviti &Linux; distribuciju "
"zainteresovanu za ovu novu stvar. Vjerujte mi -- bila sam jako uporna! Oni "
"su vjerovali da su već imali najbolje što su mogli u štampanju. Jedan razlog "
"je vjerovatno bio taj što oni (i mnogi &Linux; developeri) nikad nisu morali "
"razmišljati o tome kako napraviti podršku za obostrani ispis -- vjerovatno "
"jer nijedan nije došao ni blizu njihovih stolova."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, my attempts to make some &Linux; print publications interested in "
"&CUPS; <quote>backfired</quote> on me - one editor squeezed me into writing "
"a series on the subject myself. And this is how some people started to give "
"me the nickname <quote>CUPS Evangelist</quote>. I will not get rid of this "
"nick anytime soon, now that even the &kde; people wedged me into their "
"timeframe of releases. Oh, boy..."
msgstr ""
"Konačno, moji pokušaji da zainteresujem &Linux; štampačke publikacije "
"zainteresovane za &CUPS; <quote>mi se obilo o glavu</quote>  - jedan urednik "
"me je pritisnuo da napišem čitavu seriju na ovu temu. I tako su me ljudi "
"počeli nazivati  <quote>CUPS Evangelistom</quote>. Neću se riješiti ovog "
"nadimka u skoro vrijeme, sad kad su me ljudi iz &kde; -a vezali u njihove "
"rokove. Oh, čovječe..."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Anyway, &CUPS; is now making its way around the world and it might well "
"become a triumphal one: I am a little bit proud to have supported and "
"contributed to this from near the beginning."
msgstr ""
"U svakom slučaju, &CUPS; se sada snalazi širom svijeta i moguće je da "
"postane vodeći: pomalo sam i ponosna što sam podržavala i doprinijela ovome "
"od samog početka."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It should encourage you: even if some more experienced &Linux; users than "
"you are skeptical about it, and even if your programming skills are next to "
"zero (like mine) - there are a lot of tasks and jobs and ideas, and talent "
"that you can contribute to the Free Software community. Not least within the "
"&kde; project... ;-)"
msgstr ""
"Trebalo bi vas ohrabriti: iako postoje ljudi koji poznaju &Linux; bolje od "
"vas, i iako su vaše vještine u programiranju minorne (kao moje) - postoji "
"mnogo zadataka, poslova, ideja, i talenta kojim možete doprinijeti Free "
"Software zajednici. Ne samo u okviru &kde; projekta... ;-)"

#. Tag: title
#: final-word.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Credits"
msgstr "Zasluge"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "I'd like to thank..."
msgstr "Zahvaljujem se..."

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mike Sweet for developing &CUPS; in the first place"
msgstr "Mike Sweet-u zato što je uopće razvio &CUPS;"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Jean-Eric Cuendet for starting <application>kups</application> and "
"<application>qtcups</application>, the predecessors of &kdeprint;"
msgstr ""
"Jean-Eric Cuendet-u za pokretanje <application>kups</application> i "
"<application>qtcups</application>, koji su predhodnici &kdeprint;-a"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Michael Goffioul for doing all the hard work recently"
msgstr "Michael Goffioulu za njegov naporan rad u posljednje vrijeme"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Martin Konold for thinking twice"
msgstr "Martin Konoldu jer je o svemu dobro razmislio"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sven Guckes for teaching me a few things about the art of <quote>survival on "
"the terminal</quote> (just in case &kde; is not there ;-) )"
msgstr ""
"Sven Guckesu jer me je naučio par stvari o umjetnosti <quote>preživljavanja "
"na terminalu</quote> (u slučaju da &kde; nije bio tu ;-) )"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"...too numerous others to mention who also let me snatch bits and bytes of "
"knowledge off them"
msgstr ""
"...svima ostalima koji su mi također ponudili bitove i bajtove njihovog "
"znanja"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"and last, but not least: Tom Schwaller for encouraging me to get into "
"<quote>documentation writing</quote>"
msgstr ""
"i zadnjem, ali ne i najmanje važnom: Tom Schwalleru jer me je ohrabrio da "
"<quote>pišem dokumentaciju</quote>"

#. Tag: title
#: final-word.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr "Upozorenje"

#. Tag: para
#: final-word.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdeprint; has been developed on a system using &CUPS; 1.1.6. &kdeprint; has "
"been tested on other versions of &CUPS; and so far no incompatibilities are "
"known. By the time of writing this Handbook, &CUPS; 1.1.9 is out with a few "
"new features not yet supported by &kdeprint;. Of course you are able to "
"access these features, but you will need to bypass &kdeprint; and use the "
"&CUPS; command-line tools or edit configuration files manually. &kdeprint;'s "
"development will go on and this Handbook strives to always be the best "
"available user documentation resource for it."
msgstr ""
"&kdeprint; je razvijen na sistemu koji je koristio &CUPS; 1.1.6. &kdeprint; "
"testiran na drugim verzijama  &CUPS; i do sada nisu poznate "
"nekompatibilnosti. Do trenutka pisanja ovog Priručnika, izašao je i &CUPS; "
"1.1.9 sa novim svojstvima koji još nisu podržani od strane &kdeprint;-a. "
"Naravno, vi ste u mogućnosti da pristupite tim svojstvima, ali ćete morati "
"zaobići &kdeprint; i koristiti &CUPS; alate sa linije komandi, ili ručno "
"izmjeniti komandne datoteke. &kdeprint;ov razvoj će se nastaviti i Priručnik "
"teži ka tome da uvijek bude najbolja moguća korisnička dokumentacija za "
"njega."
